next: medci UI enhancement items #9 (interactive plotly density plot) and #10 (bookmarkable state) are parked -- both cross the golem escalation trigger (CLAUDE.md), bigger scope than the single-file quick/medium wins already shipped. Dark-mode toggle also parked (see apps/medci/README.md Follow-up -- needs a CSS-custom-properties rework first, custom layout classes use hardcoded hex). No third app currently planned.
done: 2026-08-04 -- both medci and medmc are LIVE on Connect Cloud (connect.posit.cloud), verified working. medci: root cause of 3 failed deploy attempts was Connect Cloud's native GitHub-connect flow cloning the raw repo tree directly (not an rsconnect bundle) with no renv support at all -- .Rprofile/renv/ removed entirely (PRs #11-16). Shipped UI modernization in three rounds (quick wins #1-5, medium wins #6-8, copy/download controls) plus a debounce fix for live-reactivity error-flashing, then a follow-up fix (adversarial review caught it) for a case where the plot output hadn't actually inherited the debounce and medci() was being computed twice per settle. medmc: migrated per SPEC-medmc-migration-2026-08-04.md -- not a straight port, since current RMediation::ci() is an S7 generic with no equivalent for the original's arbitrary-formula calling pattern. Reimplemented Monte Carlo + Asymptotic-Delta CI computation directly in the app, verified against the actual RMediation 1.1.3 source (contemporary with the 2014 original) after an adversarial spec review caught a point-estimate assumption error before implementation.
type: apps
last_updated: 2026-08-04

## mediation-apps

Sibling repo to the mediationverse package ecosystem, holding standalone
Shiny apps deployed to Posit Connect Cloud. Two apps live: medci
(confidence intervals for a two-coefficient indirect effect) and medmc
(Monte Carlo/Asymptotic-Delta CIs for an arbitrary user-formula), both
migrated from the legacy amplab shinyapps.io account and verified
working.

See CLAUDE.md for conventions; see mediationverse's
SPEC-shiny-apps-location-2026-08-03.md for the full design record.
